```kotlin
enum class Level(val weight: Int) {
    LOW(1), MEDIUM(5), HIGH(10);

    fun isUrgent() = this == HIGH
}
```

- Each constant is an instance and can have properties and methods.
- `Level.entries` lists all constants (prefer it over the older `values()`).
- `Level.valueOf("LOW")`, `.name` and `.ordinal` work as in Java.
- A `when` over an enum can be exhaustive with no `else`, just like a sealed type.

